{
 "title": "This website doesn't know your password",
 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "This website doesn't know your !password.!",
   "hide": true
  },
  {
   "text": "And that's a *good* thing."
  },
  {
   "text": "When you sign up, a well-built site"
  },
  {
   "text": "runs your password through a *hash:*"
  },
  {
   "text": "a *one-way* function that turns it into fixed-length gibberish."
  },
  {
   "text": "Change one letter, and the result changes !completely.!"
  },
  {
   "text": "It stores only the *hash,* plus a random *salt,*"
  },
  {
   "text": "so identical passwords look !different.!"
  },
  {
   "text": "When you log in, it hashes what you typed and *compares.*"
  },
  {
   "text": "Steal the database, and you get *hashes,* not passwords."
  },
  {
   "text": "Weak ones can still be !guessed,! one hash at a time."
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow: tomorrow, why 1 TB shows 931 GB.",
   "say": "Follow. Tomorrow: why one terabyte shows nine hundred thirty-one gigabytes."
  }
 ],
